{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article","title":"Getting Started with SwiftUI"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/SwiftUIAndUIKitEquivalents"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Recipes","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/SwiftUIAndUIKitEquivalents"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drive a SwiftUI screen’s four states with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class that owns a screen’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"type":"text","text":" and knows how to run an async load. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":" switches on that state, rendering your content only for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" case and a placeholder otherwise."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftUI","import ScreenStates","","struct ArticlesScreen: View {","    @State private var store = ScreenStateStore<[Article]>()","","    var body: some View {","        ScreenStateView(store.state, onRetry: reload) { articles in","            List(articles) { article in","                Text(article.title)","            }","        }","        .task { await reload() }","    }","","    private func reload() async {","        await store.loadCollection { try await api.fetchArticles() }","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":", runs the closure, and maps the outcome to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":" (when the result is an empty collection), or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":" shows the default Loading spinner, Empty placeholder, or Error view — with a working Retry button wired to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"type":"text","text":" — automatically."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you’d rather not wrap the whole call site in an initializer, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".screenState(_:onRetry:secondaryAction:content:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same thing as a view modifier:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["EmptyView()","    .screenState(store.state, onRetry: reload) { articles in","        List(articles) { article in Text(article.title) }","    }"]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Customizing-the-placeholders","type":"heading","text":"Customizing the placeholders"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"empty"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loading"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" view builders to fully replace the defaults:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenStateView(store.state) { articles in","    ArticleList(articles)","} empty: {","    ContentUnavailableView(\"No Articles Yet\", systemImage: \"newspaper\")","} loading: {","    ProgressView(\"Loading articles…\")","} error: { error in","    MyErrorBanner(error: error, retry: reload)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A fully custom placeholder like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MyErrorBanner"},{"type":"text","text":" can still announce transitions to VoiceOver with the same wording the default placeholders use, via "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".onAppear {","    if let announcement = state.accessibilityAnnouncement {","        AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(announcement).post()","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — your own content is what VoiceOver should read at that point — and, for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", it’s the default “Nothing Here” text; announce your own custom title directly instead if your placeholder shows one, so